المصفوفات تحول بmap وتنقى بfilter:
const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4];
const doubled = nums.map(n => n * 2);
const evens = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0);
الجمع: nums.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)

en.answer:
Arrays transform with map and filter:
const nums = [1, 2, 3, 4];
const doubled = nums.map(n => n * 2);
const evens = nums.filter(n => n % 2 === 0);
Sum: nums.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0)

answer:
fetch يرجع وعداً — انتظره ثم حوّل:
const r = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
if (!r.ok) throw new Error("فشل الطلب");
const data = await r.json();
داخل دالة عادية: ثمّة .then((r) => r.json()) — لكن async/await أوضح.

en.answer:
fetch returns a promise — await it, then parse:
const r = await fetch("https://api.example.com/data");
if (!r.ok) throw new Error("request failed");
const data = await r.json();
In a plain function use .then((r) => r.json()) — async/await is clearer.

